# {{ org_name }} — Governance Records

This repository is the official, git-native governance record for
{{ org_name }}, a 501(c)(3) nonprofit corporation incorporated in {{ state }}
(EIN: {{ ein }}{% if charter_no %}, Charter No. {{ charter_no }}{% endif %}).

It was generated from the
[Golden Records](https://github.com/US-Council/golden-records) governance-as-code
commons and is now this organization's own repository — customize it freely.

## What this repository is

The `main` branch is the current, authoritative, board-approved state of
the institution. Policies, bylaws, resolutions, minutes, and every other
governance artifact here have been through this repository's adoption
process; nothing on `main` is a draft.

## How adoption works

Governance in this repository happens through ordinary {{ platform_name }}
{{ mr_term }}s, not a separate voting system:

- **A {{ mr_abbr }} is a motion.** Opening one against `board/` or `admin/`
  branch puts a proposal in front of the people who can adopt it.
- **{{ mr_term | capitalize }} approval is a vote.** Approving a {{ mr_abbr }}
  is the electronic equivalent of voting "aye."
- **Merging is adoption.** The merge commit's timestamp is the official,
  legally operative adoption date — not the date written in the document,
  not the date of any meeting.

The full model — branch prefixes, quorum thresholds, review periods, and
the frontmatter standard every document follows — is documented in
[`GOVERNANCE.md`](GOVERNANCE.md). If this organization uses AI agents as
part of its governance workflow, [`CLAUDE.md`](CLAUDE.md) defines the hard
limits on what those agents may and may not do here — most importantly,
**agents draft; only real, named directors adopt.**

